<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  OWASP Dependency-Check suppressions.

  A suppression is a claim that a reported CVE does not apply to this project, and it is only
  honest if it says why. Every entry MUST carry:

    * the CVE it suppresses,
    * a dated note explaining why this project is not affected (wrong component matched, the
      vulnerable code path is unreachable here, fixed in the version we actually use, …),
    * where possible, an <until> date, so the claim expires and has to be re-argued rather than
      quietly outliving the reason it was made.

  An empty file is the honest starting state: nothing has been waived. If the scan fails, the first
  response is to upgrade the dependency, not to add an entry here. Suppressing a finding to make a
  build green is exactly the move ENGINEERING_STANDARDS §4 exists to prevent — the same rule the
  ArchUnit and coverage gates get.
-->
<suppressions xmlns="https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/dependency-suppression.1.3.xsd">

  <!--
    CVE-2023-5443 matched against THIS PROJECT'S OWN MODULES, not against a dependency.

    Added 2026-07-25, on the scan's first real run (the one after NVD_API_KEY was configured).
    Dependency-Check assigned every com.stoicera.einvoice artifact the CPE
    `cpe:2.3:a:e-invoice_project:e-invoice` purely because the groupId contains the word
    "einvoice", and then reported that unrelated product's CVE against all seven modules.

    This is the wrong-component case the header allows, and it is unambiguous: CVE-2023-5443 is a
    vulnerability in a different piece of software that this repository neither contains nor
    depends on. The suppression is scoped by packageUrl to our own groupId, so it can never mask a
    finding in a third-party dependency — the only thing the scan exists to find.

    No <until>: this claim does not decay, because it is about mistaken identity rather than about
    a version we might later upgrade past. Revisit only if the module coordinates change.
  -->
  <suppress>
    <notes><![CDATA[
      False positive: our own multi-module artifacts CPE-matched to the unrelated
      "e-invoice_project:e-invoice" product on a groupId substring. See the block comment above.
    ]]></notes>
    <packageUrl regex="true">^pkg:maven/com\.stoicera\.einvoice/.*$</packageUrl>
    <cve>CVE-2023-5443</cve>
  </suppress>

</suppressions>
